   286	### 4.3 Capabilities
   287	
   288	Schema 3 and later require `capabilities`. Capabilities are an audit surface,
   289	not a runtime sandbox:
   290	
   291	- `network`: `"none"` or unique host globs without whitespace or path syntax;
   292	- `filesystem`: `"repo"`, `"home-config"`, or unique portable paths;
   293	- `exec`: `"none"` or unique bare executable names;
   294	- `secrets`: `"none"` or unique non-empty secret identifiers;
   295	- `env_read`: unique environment-variable names;
   296	- `prompt_scope`: an OPTIONAL non-empty purpose statement.
   297	
   298	Missing OPTIONAL capability fields take their schema defaults.
