   403	## 8. Content hashes
   404	
   405	The Curator content hash is calculated over regular files excluding the marker
   406	itself. For each selected file in sorted protocol-path order, append:
   407	
   408	```text
   409	UTF8(path) || 0x00 || file_bytes
   410	```
   411	
   412	Join adjacent records with one additional `0x00`, hash the resulting byte
   413	string with SHA-256, encode lowercase hexadecimal, and prefix `sha256:`. The
   414	empty tree hashes the empty byte string. File mode, owner, timestamp, and
   415	filesystem-native separator are not hashed. Readers MUST reject duplicate
   416	protocol paths rather than hash one arbitrarily.
   417	
   418	### 8.1 Build-source identity
   419	
   420	The installed-tree `content_sha256` above remains unchanged and excludes root
   421	`.csk-install.json`. It MUST NOT be used as compiled-artifact identity.
   422	Compiled commands instead bind the fully validated immutable raw snapshot with
   423	algorithm identifier `curator-build-source-v1`, including every regular file
   424	and any package-provided root `.csk-install.json`.
   425	
   426	Snapshot validation MUST occur before build-cache lookup or any Go command.
   427	The snapshot MUST contain only directories and regular files; links, special
   428	files, invalid protocol paths, duplicate encoded paths, and platform path
   429	collisions are invalid. For every regular file, convert its relative protocol
   430	path to `/` separators without normalization and encode its Unicode scalar
   431	values as UTF-8. Sort those path bytes in unsigned bytewise order. Initialize
   432	SHA-256 with exact ASCII `curator-build-source-v1` followed by `0x00`, then
   433	append for each file:
   434	
   435	```text
   436	ASCII("F") || uint64be(path_byte_length) || path_utf8 ||
   437	uint64be(content_byte_length) || file_bytes
   438	```
   439	
   440	Prefix the lowercase digest with `sha256:`. An empty snapshot hashes only the
   441	domain prefix. Modes, ownership, timestamps, ACLs, and extended attributes are
   442	not inputs. Implementations MUST NOT substitute the marker-excluding content
   443	hash with an empty exclusion list: `curator-build-source-v1` is domain-separated
   444	and length-framed. The validated snapshot instance MUST remain byte-for-byte
   445	unchanged until the last build child exits.
   446	
   447	### 8.2 Go toolchain identity
   448	
   449	Every `go-v1` cache input MUST identify its operator-trusted toolchain with
   450	algorithm `curator-go-toolchain-v1`. Resolve the launcher independently of the
   451	package and before entering a package-controlled directory. It MAY be bundled
   452	with the manager or selected by trusted operator configuration, but MUST NOT
   453	come from the repository, a runtime root, project `.agents/bin`, the user
   454	`PATH`, or a manifest. Require it to be the regular executable
   455	`<resolved-goroot>/bin/go` (`bin/go.exe` on Windows), not a wrapper or an
   456	executable outside the tree being fingerprinted. A clean `go env GOROOT` probe
   457	MUST resolve to the same root.
   458	
   459	Walk `GOROOT` without following links; the root itself is not a record.
   460	Relative components MUST contain valid
   461	Unicode scalar values; encode `/`-joined paths as UTF-8 without case folding or
   462	normalization and reject duplicate encoded paths and special files. Symlinks
   463	MUST be relative, non-dangling, and resolve within `GOROOT`, and their referents
   464	have independent tree records. Sort path bytes in unsigned bytewise order.
   465	Initialize SHA-256 with exact ASCII
   466	`curator-go-toolchain-v1` followed by `0x00`, then append for every entry:
   467	
   468	```text
   469	kind || uint64be(path_byte_length) || path_utf8 ||
   470	uint64be(payload_byte_length) || payload
   471	```
   472	
   473	`kind` is ASCII `D`, `F`, or `L`; directory payload is empty, file payload is
   474	the exact bytes, and link payload is the exact UTF-8 `readlink` value. Hard
   475	links are independent regular-file records. Normalize `go version` stdout by
   476	requiring at most 4096 bytes and exactly one terminal LF, optionally preceded
   477	by CR, removing that terminator, and rejecting any other CR, LF, NUL, empty, or
   478	invalid UTF-8 content. Append it as one final `V` record with an empty path.
   479	Prefix the lowercase digest with `sha256:`.
   480	
   481	Permissions, ownership, timestamps, ACLs, and extended attributes are not hash
   482	inputs, but `bin/go` and each invoked `pkg/tool/<host>/` child MUST be regular
   483	and executable at use time. The tree MUST remain unchanged through the last
   484	child exit. The logical identity also records normalized `go_version` and
   485	`go_relpath: "bin/go"`; toolchain location is not portable identity.
   486	
   487	## 9. Compiled-artifact cache and receipts
   488	
   489	For each active build command, the manager MUST construct a logical build-input
   490	object containing schema version 1, driver, the `curator-build-source-v1`
   491	identity, `build_root`, command name, `source_dir`, native GOOS/GOARCH/tuning,
   492	the complete `curator-go-toolchain-v1` identity, and these fixed policy values:
   493	
   494	```json
   495	{
   496	  "module_mode": "vendor",
   497	  "network": "none",
   498	  "workspace": false,
   499	  "cgo": false,
   500	  "compiler_directives": "reject-nonstandard-cgo-import-dynamic-v1",
   501	  "target_mode": "native",
   502	  "link_mode": "internal",
   503	  "libgcc": "none",
   504	  "package_assembly": false,
   505	  "host_objects": false,
   506	  "telemetry": "off-private"
   507	}
   508	```
   509	
   510	The logical cache key is:
   511	
   512	```text
   513	"sha256:" || lowercase_hex(SHA-256(CCJ-1(build_input)))
   514	```
   515	
   516	`CCJ-1` is defined in `registry.md`; the input bytes have no BOM,
   517	insignificant whitespace, or terminal LF. A semantic change to arguments,
   518	environment, sandbox-relevant policy, receipt interpretation, or output rules
   519	requires a new driver identifier or an explicit versioned cache-key policy.
   520	
   521	Each immutable logical entry contains exactly one manager-derived artifact and
   522	a strict build-receipt schema 1. The receipt contains its schema version,
   523	logical cache key, the complete build input, and artifact-relative path,
   524	SHA-256, and byte length. Stored receipt bytes MUST equal `CCJ-1(receipt)`
   525	exactly. Define:
   526	
   527	```text
   528	receipt_sha256 = "sha256:" ||
   529	  lowercase_hex(SHA-256(exact_stored_receipt_bytes))
   530	```
   531	
   532	Before reuse, a reader MUST open a regular singly linked receipt without
   533	following links, recanonicalize it, and require exact stored-byte equality;
   534	recompute the build-source identity before opening the candidate; recompute and
   535	match the cache key and entire expected input; require the manager-derived
   536	artifact path; and open, bound, hash, and size-check one regular singly linked
   537	artifact without following links. It MUST reject unknown receipt fields or
   538	unsupported receipt, driver, build-source, and toolchain versions. It MUST NOT
   539	execute the artifact.
   540	
   541	Persistent reuse is permitted only below manager-created, manager-protected
   542	state resolved independently of package input. On every lookup and again under
   543	the manager-home mutation lock, the manager MUST verify ownership, private
   544	mutation permissions or DACL, containment, regular file types, and link safety
   545	for the boundary and every entry component. An implementation that cannot
   546	prove this boundary MUST disable persistent reuse. A real operation rebuilds
   547	from the revalidated snapshot into newly established protected state; dry-run
   548	reports `would-rebuild-untrusted-cache`; status is non-current. Self-consistent
   549	receipt, marker, artifact, and hash bytes do not repair or authenticate an
   550	untrusted boundary.
   551	
   552	The logical cache key, exact receipt bytes, artifact-relative path, artifact
   553	bytes/hash/size, and validation outcomes are portable. Manager-home paths,
   554	physical cache-root and driver-directory names, receipt filenames, lock and
   555	quarantine names, and storage backends are implementation-specific. A manager
   556	MUST NOT infer portable paths such as `build-cache` or `.csk-build.json`.
   557	
   558	Entries are built in operation-private staging and published atomically and
   559	immutably under the manager-home mutation lock. Receipt hashes are deterministic
   560	corruption/currentness identifiers, not signatures, MACs, attestations, or
   561	proof of provenance. The verified protected-state boundary supplies local
   562	provenance; registry audit continues to attest source, not the compiled result.
   563	
   564	Dry-run MAY validate the raw snapshot and build-root exclusion, compute build
   565	source and trusted-toolchain identity, and inspect protected entries read-only.
   566	It MUST NOT invoke `go list`, `go build`, a compiler, or linker; create Go
   567	caches, a persistent memo, a mutation lock or journal; publish, quarantine,
   568	repair, or adopt cache bytes; copy build roots into runtime; or mutate
   569	installation, registry, audit, marker, shim, adapter, or consumer state. A
   570	cache hit MUST use the same static context exclusion and, after exact receipt
   571	validation, MUST NOT run source-aware Go commands.
   572	
   573	## 10. Install markers
   574	
   575	Every installed closure node has `.csk-install.json`. Managers MUST read marker
   576	schemas 1 and 2, MUST write schema 2 on every installation mutation, and MAY
   577	continue to regard a valid marker-v1 installation as current for a schema 1
   578	through 5 package. Marker v1 retains its existing shape and meaning.
   579	
   580	Marker v2 permits `skill_schema_version` through 6 and requires sorted
   581	`build_roots` and a `builds` object, including empty values for installations
   582	without active compiled commands. `build_source` is REQUIRED exactly when
   583	`builds` is non-empty and MUST otherwise be absent. Each lexically ordered
   584	`builds` entry records driver, logical cache key, `receipt_sha256`, artifact
   585	SHA-256, and manager-derived artifact-relative path. A build shim MUST target
   586	the immutable cache artifact selected by the effective plan and marker, not the
   587	commit-keyed script runtime store.
   588	
   589	`locale` is always present and is a string or `null`. Required set-like arrays
   590	are always arrays, including when empty.
   591	
   592	The following arrays are set-like and writers sort them by Unicode scalar
   593	value: `agents`, `commands`, `dependencies`, `files`, `requirements`,
   594	`runtime_roots`, `build_roots`, `requirers`, `activation.commands`, and every
   595	MCP agent list. Writers sort `builds` keys by Unicode scalar value. Object
   596	member order and whitespace are not significant.
   597	
   598	An installation is current only when the marker schema is supported; ref kind,
   599	ref, commit, locale, agents, activation, substitution, MCP findings, and
   600	attestation match the effective plan; and the installed content hash matches
   601	`content_sha256`. For a build-enabled marker, currentness additionally requires
   602	the declared build roots and static context exclusion to match; the fully
   603	validated raw snapshot's `build_source` to match the effective plan and every
   604	receipt input; each logical cache key and manager-derived artifact path to
   605	match; and every referenced receipt/artifact to validate below a currently
   606	verified manager-protected boundary. A missing raw snapshot, prompt-visible or
   607	runtime-copied build-root file, untrusted boundary, corrupt receipt/artifact,
   608	wrong target or toolchain, or mismatched source identity makes the installation
   609	non-current. Repair MUST rebuild from a revalidated snapshot into protected
   610	state rather than adopt candidate bytes.
   611	
   612	Unsupported or unreadable markers are not current. A moved tag is a warning,
   613	or an error under strict-tag policy.
   614	
   615	The marker and its referenced receipt hashes are not signatures and MUST NOT be
   616	used as authorization tokens or provenance proof. Registry attestations are
   617	reverified from signed records when fresh trust is required.
   618	
   619	## 11. Adapter ledger
   620	
   621	Every managed adapter root contains `.csk-managed.json` conforming to
   622	`adapter-ledger-v1.schema.json`. `entries` is a sorted unique list of skill
   623	names owned by the manager in that adapter root. A manager MUST remove only
   624	entries in its preceding ledger and MUST fail rather than overwrite an
   625	unmanaged conflicting entry.

